include g474.tdc
diagram d "ZLI: the edge preempts a masked SysTick ISR"
letter "D"
num value "55, 59 to 65 cycles"
num share "no tail in 1M"
num path "zero-latency ISR, idle"
what "A zero-latency IRQ has a priority above the BASEPRI threshold. It preempts the SysTick ISR and any locked section at once. In exchange it must not call the kernel, so it cannot wake a thread."
evidence "ZLI max 65 cycles in 1 million samples. The direct path reaches 1633."
evidence "Its second mode (59, 0.60 %) is the same cache effect as on the other paths (card B)."
src "irq-baseline-1m/20261029T012553Z"

axis "cycles after the edge" -300..300

mask -300..300 "BASEPRI: masks kernel IRQs, not the ZLI" : The SysTick ISR holds BASEPRI. The lock value is _EXC_IRQ_DEFAULT_PRIO (include/zephyr/arch/arm/cortex_m/exception.h:53). The ZLI priority is above it.
at -300
tick 300 "SysTick ISR" : The SysTick ISR runs and holds BASEPRI.
hw 30 "stacking" : The ZLI priority is above the BASEPRI threshold, so the exception entry starts at once. Pin, EXTI, NVIC and stacking; the CPU is awake.
zli 14? "+14" : The same 14 cycles as in card A. Where in the path these cycles go is not measured.
zli miss 15 "miss" : Cold cache: the SysTick code just ran. Length: an estimate, so that the total is the max of 65 cycles.
zli 6 : The ISR reads TIM2->CNT.
at 75
tick 225 "SysTick ISR continues" : The SysTick ISR continues after the ZLI returns.

@t0_1 edge "edge" at 0
@t0_2 stamp "CNT read" at 65
span 0..65 "65 cycles: the max, measured" !
